    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1970s, developer Hawaiian Islands Land Company turned the barren Kula Kai into a luxury resort destination.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/hawaii_wailea-makena"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wailea’s master‑planned resort covers 1,500 acres on Maui’s sunny southern leeward coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wailea%2C_Hawaii"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community was developed in 1971 by a partnership of Alexander & Baldwin and Northwestern Mutual.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wailea%2C_Hawaii"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wailea is bordered by Makena to the south, Kihei to the north, the Pacific to the west and Haleakalā to the east.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
